<speak>I expect to be away for a short family visit, but the itinerary is still being settled. My wife is coordinating with her sister, and every time they speak, somebody suggests another lunch or another place to visit. I have deliberately not filled the trip with business appointments. If I do that, I will come back having had no proper break. I should still be able to read messages, but I do not want ordinary telephone calls arriving while we are out with the family. Better to arrange those beforehand, or wait until I am back at my normal desk and not watching the clock.</speak>